            <ArticleTitle>The Iranian version of Angina Pectoris characteristics questionnaire: reliability assessment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>694-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1365-2702.2008.02573.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIMS" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To evaluate internal consistency and test-retest reliability of the Iranian version of the Angina Pectoris characteristics questionnaire.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">To evaluate symptoms in patients with Angina Pectoris, the Iranian version of the Angina Pectoris characteristics questionnaire was created by combining items from Modified Rose Questionnaire, Short Form-McGill Questionnaire and the Accompanying Symptom Checklist. The Angina Pectoris characteristics questionnaire has been developed and validated recently although it required assessment of its reliability.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Reliability study using test and retest.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">One hundred and ten coronary heart disease patients with Angina Pectoris were included. The test-retest reliability of the instrument was estimated for measurement after 15 days.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The analysis of the result indicated that internal consistency was found adequate at both assessments (Cronbach's alpha = 0.65) for test and retest. There was no significant difference between test and retest. The intra-class correlation coefficient ranged from 0.76-0.98.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The Angina Pectoris characteristics questionnaire is a reliable instrument for the assessment of Angina Pectoris characteristics in a Persian population.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RELEVANCE TO CLINICAL PRACTICE" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The Angina Pectoris characteristics questionnaire can be used with confidence in Iranian coronary heart disease patients for Assessing Angina Pectoris symptom.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
